:null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.1772616935055289,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.238339185511784,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.11930077538143714,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.016767841890262813,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":71.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006032032505416765,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0232,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":15.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"RenaissanceRe Holdings Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, provides reinsurance and insurance products in the United States and internationally. The company operates through Property, and Casualty and Specialty segments. The Property segment writes property catastrophe excess of loss reinsurance contracts to insure insurance and reinsurance companies against natural and man-made catastrophes, including hurricanes, earthquakes, typhoons, and tsunamis, as well as winter storms, freezes, floods, fires, windstorms, tornadoes, explosions, and acts of terrorism; and other property class of products, such as proportional reinsurance, property per risk, property reinsurance, binding facilities, and regional U.S. multi-line reinsurance. The Casualty and Specialty segment writes various classes of products, such as directors and officers, medical malpractice, transactional liability, and professional indemnity; automobile and employer's liability, casualty clash, umbrella or excess casualty, workers' compensation, and general liability; financial and mortgage guaranty, political risk, surety, and trade credit; and accident and health, agriculture, aviation, construction, cyber, energy, marine, satellite, and terrorism. The company distributes products and services primarily through intermediaries. It invests in and manages funds. RenaissanceRe Holdings Ltd. was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in Pembroke, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin Joseph O'Donnell | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $7.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $12.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $75K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["RenaissanceRe Holdings Ltd. is a large-cap financial services business with a $14.0B market cap on $12.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 30% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 34\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 11.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.020551199809933487},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"RNR vs. WRB: Which Stock Is the Better Value Option?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025760/rnr-vs-wrb-which-stock-is-the-better-value-option?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3025760","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793979603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":